From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 14:27:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Implement slot assignment (named slots, fallback, ::slotted)

The composition half of shadow DOM. flush_slot_assignments runs each
resolve before styling (::slotted needs fresh edges) over a new
shadow_roots registry: per tree, collect slots in pre-order (light
walk - nested trees own their own slots), name->slot first-wins with
"" as the default, then distribute host light children (elements by
slot attr, text to the default slot; comments aren't slottables).
assigned_slot lives on Node rather than ElementData because text
nodes carry assignment too.

Consumers: flat_children()/the flat iteration macros/methods now
yield assigned nodes for slots (children = fallback, shown only when
nothing is assigned - the take-based push_hoisted collector needed
the same branch or it rendered fallback alongside assigned content);
stylo's traversal_parent/inheritance_parent hang assigned nodes off
their slot; Traverser reads flat_children so hosts/slots/normal nodes
all traverse uniformly; assigned_slot() + is_html_slot_element() are
overridden - the selectors crate debug-asserts the latter and
::slotted() matching is dead without them. slot{display:contents}
already ships in the UA sheet, so layout projection comes free.

Invalidation: host child-list mutations already damage the host;
`slot` attr changes on a host's light child and `name` changes on a
slot damage the affected host explicitly. Reparenting and removal
clear assigned_slot so recycled slab ids can't resurrect stale
flat-tree edges. A slot's box parent lays out the slot's assigned
nodes, but those are the host's DOM children, so a change to them never
damaged that parent; under incremental layout a slottable added after
the first layout never got a box. flush_slot_assignments compares each
slot's assignment with the previous one and stamps CONSTRUCT_BOX on the
slots that changed.

assignedNodes() and assignedSlot need fresh assignments, so they flush
on every call. A dirty flag set by the mutations that can reshape
assignment (child-list changes, slot/name attribute writes,
attach_shadow) lets the flush no-op between changes, so a slotchange
scan over S slots no longer costs S full recomputes, and steady-state
resolves skip the walk. It starts set so the first flush always runs.
